+## Failure during session setup
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the turn calls `onError(session, error)` with the original session and error, then `afterSession(session)`, and rejects to the caller with that same error when those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model-response work runs. `afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, not proof that setup succeeded: it must tolerate missing or partially allocated resources, and a deployer needing allocation state must track it in its hooks. ([validated by: reports a beforeSession failure and cleans up partial setup before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
